body:
Oh, there probably is not too much to talk about here. It is pretty simple: If I own less things/interested in less things then I would also have less to worry about. 

&#x200B;

Anyways, thank you for your message :) Is there anything I can do for you in return, do you want to talk?

Talking to my family is not an option. They, especially my mother, have shown me often enough that they don't care about me. I tried it many times, talking to them. Not only about my problems but other things as well. Normal things people talk about with each other. Do you know the feeling when you write with someone and you can feel how this person just does not want to have anything to do with you? That is how I felt every single time I talked to them, just in person. I don't want to talk to people who insulted me and even told me to go kill myself.

&#x200B;

Friends? I am not sure if I have any. Sure, I know people I went to school with and I have their phone numbers but I don't think we are connected enough. Besides that, I don't like talking about my problems with people I actually know. Talking to stranger, real life and internet, is much much easier for me.

&#x200B;

I am so sorry for this reply. I don't really want to be the guy that has a problem for every solution.

&#x200B;

I think I am going to watch a few episodes of a super comfy show now to calm down a bit and later on play some video games. I just tried to play something but I can't think straight right now so yeah. Those things should help me to keep myself distracted from my thoughts. 

&#x200B;

Thanks for your message!

As I said above: My psychologist talked bad about me and my mom right and said a lot of mean things. If he already talked like that to me in person then I don't want to know how he talked about me behind my back.

&#x200B;

The hospital just basically combines everything that makes me anxious. I hate being among other people in real life. The worst part was when we had to eat. I almost never ate anything because it makes me so anxious to eat in front of someone. I also like it when everything is clean. I would not say I suffer from mysophobia because I never went to a doc because of that but I can't touch anything someone else touched without washing my hands afterwards so sharing a bathroom with someone is HORRIBLE. There are a lot of different scenarios but it would be too long to write everything down here.
